  "answer": "The planned availabilities differ significantly in timing, target audience, and risk. The Advanced OCR Pipeline is scheduled for general release in August 2026 (v2.8.0, target release August 25, 2026) [NL-014#NL-014-S03]. Its plan availability is tiered: included natively in the Enterprise plan, offered as a paid add-on for Growth plans ($500/month), and not supported on the Starter plan [NL-014#NL-014-S06]. The WorkflowCoach public beta is officially targeted for September 2026 (v2.9.0, target release September 29, 2026) and made available to all active Growth and Enterprise accounts [NL-014#NL-014-S03][NL-014#NL-014-S05]. However, due to dependencies on the Advanced OCR Pipeline and permission synchronization, and internal engineering estimates, the public beta may slip to November 2026, with an internal contingency plan aligned on that slip while maintaining the September official external messaging [NL-014#NL-014-S05][NL-015#NL-015-S05]. In contrast, the Teams connector is planned strictly for Q4 2026 (v2.11.0, November release) and is currently under active design and planning, with a restricted pilot beginning in October 2026 for selected financial and healthcare enterprise accounts [NL-014#NL-014-S07].\n\nANSWER_STATUS: answer\nUSED_MEMORY_CLAIMS: none",
